Major Revisions
(24)
A major revision of a graduate research course may include but is not limited to the following:
the introduction of core coursework subjects;
changes to more than two existing core or core choice subjects;
a change to the name of the graduate research course;
any changes in admission criteria including English Language Proficiency (ELP) per the
English Language Entry Requirements Policy
;
any changes in examination requirements; or
any change which involves joint enrolment with another institution.
(25)
All proposals for a major revision must be submitted for review as follows:
Dean (or nominee) for endorsement (discipline-specific courses only);
the Board of Graduate Research for endorsement; and
the Academic Board for approval.
